---
/**
 * Request path and storage boundaries. Local or remote agents arrive over HTTP,
 * the CLI or eleven MCP tools; grants and bounded policy decide what is
 * durable and what lives in RAM; the stored schema is versioned.
 */
---

<figure
  class="figure"
  tabindex="0"
  aria-label="Architecture and stored schema diagram"
>
  <svg
    class="diagram"
    viewBox="0 0 1200 700"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
  >
    <title id="arch-title">instantKV architecture and stored schema</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      HTTP, CLI and MCP clients authenticate with a scoped token. Grants and
      bounded policy route durable knowledge and checkpoints to an embedded redb
      database and optional scratch to RAM with TTL and FIFO eviction. The
      stored record carries a namespace, key, revision, value, TTL and checksum;
      a checkpoint commits a capsule and the session latest pointer in one
      transaction.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <linearGradient
        id="flow-spectrum-architecture"
        x1="0"
        y1="0"
        x2="1"
        y2="0"
      >
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#2359a6" />
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#2359a6" />
      </linearGradient>
    </defs>

    <text class="d-index" x="20" y="34">
      02 / ARCHITECTURE
    </text>
    <text class="d-index" x="1180" y="34" text-anchor="end">
      RUST · TOKIO · AXUM · REDB
    </text>
    <path class="d-rule--faint" d="M20 46H1180" />

    <!-- clients -->
    <text class="d-index" x="20" y="96">
      AGENT CLIENTS
    </text>
    <rect class="d-node" x="20" y="112" width="210" height="72" />
    <text class="d-label" x="40" y="142">
      HTTP
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="40" y="164">
      bearer token, conditional writes
    </text>

    <rect class="d-node" x="20" y="204" width="210" height="72" />
    <text class="d-label" x="40" y="234">
      CLI
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="40" y="256">
      records, checkpoints, bench
    </text>

    <rect class="d-node" x="20" y="296" width="210" height="88" />
    <text class="d-label" x="40" y="326">
      MCP · 7 TOOLS
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="40" y="348">
      store, list, get, delete,
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="40" y="366">
      checkpoint, restore, health
    </text>

    <!-- policy -->
    <text class="d-index" x="330" y="96">
      BOUNDED POLICY
    </text>
    <rect class="d-node d-node--key" x="330" y="112" width="240" height="272" />
    <text class="d-label" x="354" y="142">
      GRANTS
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="164">
      token → namespaces
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="180">
      per-operation rights
    </text>
    <text class="d-label" x="354" y="222">
      LIMITS
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="244">
      record, key and value size
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="260">
      namespace quotas, restore budget
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="276">
      admission control
    </text>
    <text class="d-label" x="354" y="318">
      CHECKSUM
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="340">
      read verified against the write
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="354" y="360">
      every read is accounted
    </text>

    <!-- storage -->
    <text class="d-index" x="670" y="96">
      STORAGE
    </text>
    <rect
      class="d-node d-node--store"
      x="670"
      y="112"
      width="300"
      height="126"
    />
    <text class="d-label" x="694" y="142">
      DURABLE · REDB
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="164">
      shared + private knowledge
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="180">
      immutable capsules
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="196">
      session latest pointer
    </text>
    <text class="d-value" x="694" y="220">
      no TTL by default
    </text>

    <rect class="d-node" x="670" y="258" width="300" height="126" />
    <text class="d-label" x="694" y="288">
      SCRATCH · RAM
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="310">
      optional namespace
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="326">
      TTL and FIFO eviction
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="694" y="342">
      cleared on restart
    </text>
    <text class="d-value" x="694" y="366">
      disposable notes
    </text>

    <!-- flows -->
    <path
      class="d-flow--spectrum d-pulse"
      stroke="url(#flow-spectrum-architecture)"
      d="M230 148C280 148 286 200 330 200"
    />
    <path
      class="d-flow--spectrum d-pulse"
      stroke="url(#flow-spectrum-architecture)"
      d="M230 240C280 240 286 240 330 240"
    />
    <path
      class="d-flow--spectrum d-pulse"
      stroke="url(#flow-spectrum-architecture)"
      d="M230 340C280 340 286 288 330 288"
    />
    <text class="d-note" x="278" y="176" text-anchor="middle">
      auth
    </text>
    <path class="d-flow--write d-pulse" d="M570 176C620 176 626 176 670 176" />
    <path class="d-flow--write d-pulse" d="M570 240C620 240 626 320 670 320" />
    <text class="d-note" x="622" y="164" text-anchor="middle">
      durable
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="622" y="292" text-anchor="middle">
      ram
    </text>

    <!-- schema inset -->
    <rect
      class="d-rule"
      x="1000"
      y="112"
      width="180"
      height="272"
      stroke-dasharray="2 6"
    />
    <text class="d-index" x="1020" y="140">
      SCHEMA 1
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1020" y="170">
      record
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="188">
      namespace
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="204">
      key
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="220">
      revision
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="236">
      value
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="252">
      ttl · checksum
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1020" y="288">
      capsule
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="306">
      goal · constraints
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="322">
      unfinished · next
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="338">
      references → keys
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1034" y="354">
      session latest
    </text>

    <!-- transaction note -->
    <path class="d-rule--faint" d="M20 440H1180" />
    <text class="d-index" x="20" y="468">
      ONE TRANSACTION
    </text>
    <rect
      class="d-node d-node--private"
      x="20"
      y="482"
      width="560"
      height="80"
    />
    <text class="d-label" x="44" y="514">
      CAPSULE + SESSION LATEST POINTER
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="44" y="538">
      a checkpoint write commits the immutable capsule and moves the session
      pointer together
    </text>

    <text class="d-index" x="620" y="468">
      READ PATH
    </text>
    <rect class="d-node" x="620" y="482" width="560" height="80" />
    <text class="d-label" x="644" y="514">
      EXACT KEY OR PREFIX, NO MODEL CALLS
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="644" y="538">
      restore reports which referenced record changed or went missing
    </text>

    <path class="d-rule--faint" d="M20 600H1180" />
    <text class="d-note" x="20" y="626">
      Stack: Rust with Tokio and Axum; redb supplies durable transactions
      without a separate database service.
    </text>
    <text class="d-note" x="1180" y="626" text-anchor="end">
      one binary · one config · one data directory
    </text>
  </svg>

  <div class="diagram-legend">
    <span class="k-spectrum">
      <i></i> authenticated request
    </span>
    <span class="k-write">
      <i></i> durable write
    </span>
    <span>dashed frame: stored schema, version 1</span>
  </div>
</figure>
